          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_Commonwealth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "internal_fragmentation",
      "layer": "military_security",
      "description": "The Sturlung Age (c. 1220–1262) saw Iceland's major chieftain families wage brutal civil warfare; the Sturlungar and Haukdælar factions devastated farms, burned settlements, and killed hundreds, destroying the Commonwealth's consensual political culture",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
          "id": "Q62389",
          "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q62389"
